<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Song Ma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ma River is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> and north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, about 500 km long, flowing south-east through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanh-hoa">Thanh Hoa</a> province to the Gulf of Tonkin. Its lower valley is one of the cradles of Vietnamese civilisation, home with the Red River delta to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dong-son-culture">Dong Son culture</a>, whose type site lies on its bank. Thanh Hoa was later the home region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Le Loi</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyen lords</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ma-river.jpg" alt="Ma River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: vi:thành viên:Nga-Việt Nguyễn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SongMa.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
